# Stack above the page ground

`AuroraBand` is `position: fixed` with `z-0`. A positioned `z-0` layer paints **above** in-flow content that has no `position` and no z-index. A footer, button, or bar left in normal flow at the bottom of the page disappears under the grain, even when it comes later in the DOM.

- The ground stays `z-0` and `pointer-events-none`. Do not raise it.
- The sheet (terminal, settings, kit stage) is one `relative z-10` wrapper. Every control that must stay visible lives **inside** that wrapper.
- A floating control is `absolute z-20` inside that wrapper, not a sibling of the aurora. A bottom bar, if there is one, is the same: `relative z-20` and an opaque `--bg-*`.
- Portaled overlays (dialog, drawer, toast) use `z-[60]` or higher so they sit above the sheet.

```tsx
<div className="relative isolate flex h-dvh flex-col">
  <AuroraBand />
  <div className="relative z-10 flex min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col">
    {/* header, columns */}
    <div className="absolute right-4 bottom-4 z-20">{/* Demo */}</div>
  </div>
</div>
```
